Lab 6: Testing Camel Routes
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Set up unit tests for Apache Camel routes using the JUnit framework
Use CamelTestSupport to isolate and test individual routes effectively
Simulate input data and validate output results in Camel route testing
Implement mock endpoints to verify message flow and transformations
Apply testing best practices for integration routes in enterprise applications
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts (routes, endpoints, processors)
Familiarity with Java programming language
Knowledge of Maven build tool and dependency management
Understanding of unit testing concepts
Experience with JUnit testing framework (basic level)
Your machine needs the following installed. Verify each with the commands shown:

java -version
mvn -version
Expected output should show Java 11 or higher and Maven 3.6 or higher. If either is missing, install them first:

# Debian/Ubuntu example
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-11-jdk maven
All other dependencies (Apache Camel 3.x, JUnit 5, camel-test-junit5, camel-mock) are declared in the pom.xml you will create in Task 1, and Maven will download them automatically the first time you build.

